# Doodle quest — environment template.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The app currently needs no environment variables at all: the Supabase project and
# its three edge functions were decommissioned in S0.2, and nothing in src/ makes a
# network call any more. This file is kept as the template for whatever the future
# server needs.
#
# Rule that must survive that change: every variable Vite exposes to the browser is
# prefixed VITE_, and Vite inlines it into the bundle at build time. Anything with a
# VITE_ prefix is therefore PUBLIC. Never put a service-role key, an API secret or any
# other credential behind a VITE_ prefix — server-side secrets belong in the server
# process's own environment.
#
# Old Supabase variables (VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID, VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY,
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL) are gone. If they are still present in your local .env they are
# inert; nothing reads them.
